            <exercise>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        The Babylonian tablet YBC7289 gives an approximation for <m>\sqrt{2}</m> as <m>1,24,51,10</m>. Calculate this as an exact fraction (noting how you know order of magnitude) in our modern number system. When you plug this into a caclulator, how accurate is it?
                    </p>
                </statement>
